            "review_title": "Review at GoBurger",
            "review_text": "Johnny K\nPhu Quoc Island, Vietnam26 contributions\n0\nNot too bad, could be better.\nSep 2014 • Family\nIt was a little hard to find since the \"restaurant\" is soo tiny. Not much seating available. Burger was decent for the price but if you are craving a juicy burger then it will leave you disappointed. It was the first time I've ever been served food on a piece of wrapping paper (no tray no basket) so it was a little bit of a shock but it makes sense to keep costs down and no dishes to worry about.\nChicken nuggets were decent but you can tell they cooked it in old oil. \n\nStaff was friendly enough but felt like they were rushing me out to fill my spot with new customers which makes sense since the place is so small.\n\nMy recommendation? If you are cashed strapped and have to have a burger then this is the place to go, but if you Jonesing for a good burger then there are better places.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten October 31, 2014",
            "rating": 5.0,
